# Target: Infineon TLE9879-2QXA40

MOTIX™ Embedded Power IC for 3-phase BLDC/PMSM motor control.

## Silicon

- Core: ARM Cortex-M3 @ up to 40 MHz
- Flash (IROM1): 124 KiB code; IROM2: 4 KiB (data/NVM per DFP layout)
- RAM (IRAM1): 6 KiB; IRAM2: 20 B
- Debug: SWD (Segger J-Link on eval kits)
- Notable blocks: CCU6 (PWM), BDRV (3-phase gate driver), ADC1/ADC2, CSA, GPT12, Timer2/3, LIN, UART, SSC/SPI, DMA, PMU, WDT, NVIC

## Toolchain (preferred)

1. Keil µVision5 / MDK + pack **Infineon.TLE987x_DFP**
2. **Config Wizard for MOTIX™ MCU** (Infineon Developer Center) for clock/peripheral XML → generated init
3. Segger J-Link for flash/debug

Device select in Pack Installer / new project: **TLE9879-2QXA40** (not older TLE9879QXA40 unless matching silicon).

## Agent behavior

- Prefer Infineon SDK / Config Wizard APIs over bare register hacks unless registers are required.
- Respect 6 KiB RAM: no large buffers, heap, or printf stacks by default.
- Motor/PWM/BDRV changes must consider dead-time, shoot-through, and overcurrent paths.
- Do not invent pack paths or register names; use `tle987x.h` / SVD / SDK headers from the DFP when present.
